Origin
------
Parts of this software are derived from ERPparam
  https://github.com/voytekresearch/ERPparam
  commit 98e52e3bf538031987ce2986bd93141efc475002 (October 2025)
  Copyright 2017 Voytek Lab (UC San Diego), the ERPparam authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

ERPparam is itself derived from FOOOF / specparam
  https://github.com/fooof-tools/fooof
  Copyright 2017 Voytek Lab (UC San Diego), the FOOOF authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  Reference: Donoghue T, Haller M, Peterson EJ, et al. Parameterizing neural
  power spectra into periodic and aperiodic components. Nature Neuroscience
  23, 1655-1665 (2020). doi:10.1038/s41593-020-00744-x

Modifications
-------------
- October 2026: package renamed from ERPparam to evoparam; all code and
  material specific to power-spectrum fitting (tutorials, examples,
  motivations, documentation site, spectral example data, FOOOF wording
  in docstrings, upstream download address, upstream metadata and contacts)
  removed or rewritten for evoked-response parameterization.
- Later changes are recorded in CHANGELOG.md and in the git history of this repository.

Code derived from SciPy
-----------------------
evoparam/models/_trf.py is derived from the trust-region reflective solver of
SciPy (scipy/optimize/_lsq/trf.py and scipy/optimize/_lsq/common.py)
  https://github.com/scipy/scipy
  version 1.18.1
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License, reproduced below
Changes: only the bounded, dense, linear-loss path with x_scale="jac" and the
exact trust-region solver is kept, and the Jacobian can be reduced by a QR
factorisation once per evaluation (the file header lists the changes).

